{"id":"e16t3","name":"Typical Reorder Interval","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The CRM team wants to know how often customers come back. You have the table <b>purchases</b> with the columns <code>purchase_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code> and <code>purchased_at</code> (timestamp).</p>\n<p>Several purchases on the same calendar day count as <b>one</b> visit. The <b>interval</b> between two consecutive visits of a customer is the number of days between their dates.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return, for every customer with at least <code>3</code> visits, the columns <code>customer_id</code>, <code>visits</code>, <code>median_interval_days</code> (the median of the intervals, computed with <code>PERCENTILE_CONT(0.5)</code>, rounded to 1 decimal) and <code>max_interval_days</code>, sorted by <code>median_interval_days</code>, then <code>customer_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>purchases</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>purchase_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>purchased_at</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-01 10:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-01 18:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-04 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-14 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-03 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-05 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-15 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>3</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>3</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>visits</th><th>median_interval_days</th><th>max_interval_days</th></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>2.0</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>6.5</td><td>10</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["LAG","écart en jours","PERCENTILE_CONT","un seul achat par jour"],"minutes":15,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"purchases":{"columns":[["purchase_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["purchased_at","TIMESTAMP"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2026-03-01 10:00:00"],[2,1,"2026-03-01 18:00:00"],[3,1,"2026-03-04 09:00:00"],[4,1,"2026-03-14 09:00:00"],[5,2,"2026-03-01 09:00:00"],[6,2,"2026-03-03 09:00:00"],[7,2,"2026-03-05 09:00:00"],[8,2,"2026-03-15 09:00:00"],[9,3,"2026-03-01 09:00:00"],[10,3,"2026-03-02 09:00:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","visits","median_interval_days","max_interval_days"],"rows":[[2,4,2.0,10],[1,3,6.5,10]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"purchases":{"columns":[["purchase_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["purchased_at","TIMESTAMP"]],"rows":[[1,9,"2026-02-27 23:59:00"],[2,9,"2026-02-28 00:01:00"],[3,9,"2026-03-01 12:00:00"],[4,9,"2026-03-01 13:00:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","visits","median_interval_days","max_interval_days"],"rows":[[9,3,1.0,1]]}}],"hidden_n":7,"hidden":"","solution":""}